            <ArticleTitle>Anaphylaxis to ibuprofen in a 12-year-old boy.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2012-007873</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2012007873</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory (NSAIDs) drugs are a group of medications acting through cyclooxygenase  (COX-1) and cyclooxygenase  (COX-2) enzymes inhibition. Hypersensitivity reactions to NSAIDs, although not rare, are poorly characterised and often go undiagnosed especially in children. We present in this paper a case of ibuprofen anaphylaxis that exemplifies the challenges involved in diagnosis and management of hypersensitivity reactions to NSAIDs.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
